From 84c8d296d66e6418606a8c21542f08466401fb52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Duron27 <duron27@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 02:25:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Non-pausing chat, player-to-player trade window

- chat: no UI mode (game keeps running); fix lock-up caused by polling the lagging I.UI.getMode()
- trade: avatar menu entry, shared deal with both inventories visible, revisioned accept, MpTradeExec in global
- relay: forward trade_* messages between any two players
- bot: accepts trades; test hooks for the UI

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 multiplayer/README.md                         |  25 +-
 multiplayer/debug/scripts/mp_debug/give.lua   |  12 +-
 .../debug/scripts/mp_debug/maxstats.lua       |  22 +-
 multiplayer/mod/scripts/mp/global.lua         |  40 +++
 multiplayer/mod/scripts/mp/player.lua         |  50 ++-
 multiplayer/mod/scripts/mp/trade.lua          | 299 ++++++++++++++++++
 multiplayer/server/owner_bot.py               |  14 +-
 multiplayer/server/relay.py                   |   6 +
 8 files changed, 429 insertions(+), 39 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 multiplayer/mod/scripts/mp/trade.lua

diff --git a/multiplayer/README.md b/multiplayer/README.md
index 2b3b7cae51..0e4d9f3368 100644
--- a/multiplayer/README.md
+++ b/multiplayer/README.md
@@ -8,18 +8,21 @@
 Run: `multiplayer/run-test.sh [path/to/openmw]`, then load a save. Watch `openmw.log` for `[mp]` lines.
 Protocol: one JSON object per line, `{"t":"state","name","cell","pos":[x,y,z],"yaw"}`; the server adds `id`.
 
-## Per-player worlds and groups (stage 3)
+## How it works
 Every player keeps their **own** world; nothing a group member does changes yours.
-Only players in the same *group* (Options -> Scripts -> Multiplayer; default group `lobby`, empty = solo) see each other:
-- Members appear as stand-in NPCs with their look and gear (visible only when you share a cell).
-- If a member has an NPC/creature **alive** that is dead or missing in **your** world, you get a *proxy* copy named
-  `Name [Alice's world]`: its own record, no script, no AI, can't be talked to. You can fight it; the damage is sent to
-  Alice, whose real actor takes it (so she can finish her quest) while your world stays untouched.
-  Proxies mirror the owner's actor position and health. Hits on a proxy never give you a bounty (best effort).
-- Leaving the group (or the member disconnecting) removes their avatar and all their proxies.
+- **Presence:** everyone online appears as a stand-in NPC (look + gear) when you share a cell. Activate one for a menu:
+  invite to party, accept/decline, leave party, **trade**.
+- **Parties (max 3):** shared party chat, health/magicka/fatigue panel, and *proxies*: if a member has an NPC/creature
+  alive that is dead or missing in your world you get a marked copy `Name [Alice's world]` (own record, no script, no AI).
+  Damage you do to it is applied to the owner's real actor, so they can finish their quest. Your world is untouched.
+- **Chat:** Enter or Y opens the input (the game keeps running); Enter sends, Tab switches Global/Party.
+  `/accept [name]`, `/decline [name]`, `/leave`, `/g text`, `/p text`.
+- **Trade:** both inventories are shown (like a merchant's goods). Click to add an item to the deal, right-click adds
+  the whole stack; both players must accept the same revision. Items are recreated from their record id on the receiving
+  side (condition/enchant charge reset; runtime-generated items can't be traded). It is not atomic across a crash.
 
-Test with one client: `server/owner_bot.py [--hurt <contentfile>:<index>]` pretends to be a member owning a scrib
-that doesn't exist in your world, and applies/prints damage you do to it.
+Test with one client: `run-test.sh [--cheat]` starts the relay, a "Bot" player (auto-accepts party invites and trades,
+owns a scrib that doesn't exist in your world) and OpenMW. `server/owner_bot.py --help` lists bot options.
 
 Not done: members' attacks on you, shared fights where both worlds have the actor alive, container contents,
-weather/time, quest sync (by design none), proxies for actors that are alive-but-unloaded in your world.
+weather/time, proxies for actors that are alive-but-unloaded in your world, trade of enchanted/generated items.
